1	//! sieve.rs — a Dixon / quadratic-sieve core over the folded numeral tapes.
2	//!
3	//! The sub-exponential arm for the HARD shape: a factor that is large, far from
4	//! the root, and not smooth, where trial, rho, the frontier and p±1 all fail.
5	//! It collects relations a^2 == q (mod N) whose q factors over a small-prime
6	//! base, finds a subset of relations whose exponents are all even (a linear
7	//! dependency over GF(2)), and from the resulting X^2 == Y^2 (mod N) takes
8	//! gcd(X - Y, N). Value-sized arithmetic (a^2 mod N, the gcd) runs on the shared
9	//! folded kernel; the base primes and the GF(2) matrix are machine words.
